     Settings > About phone. The row's label comes from R.string.voltage_version
     (VoltageVersionPreference.kt:47); its value is the org.voltage.version
     property, which is the VoltageOS platform version (6.1) and cannot be
     redefined from a product layer - see the note in config/branding.mk.

     So the label says what the value IS. Calling it "BestROM version" would
     display 6.1 as BestROM's version, which it is not: BestROM's own version
     is in ro.bestrom.version.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="voltage_version">Platform base version</string>
</resources>
